\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces What the layer sees: the logits of the candidates of the last 10 frames, just before its decision for frame 101 of a sequence, with the two Otsu splits $t_1$ (dashed line) and $t_2$ (solid line). Plain light bars: background; hatched bars: uncertain; plain dark bars: confident. The top axis gives the detector score that matches each logit. (a) MOT17-02 with the published YOLOX-X detections: most foreground candidates are confident, and the stream is clean, so the tracker keeps its settings. (b) KITTI sequence 0001 with RT-DETR-L: many candidates are uncertain, and the stream is noisy, so the layer chooses the candidates and sets the thresholds. All values are those of the frozen layer in the runs of Sect.~\ref {sec:results}}}{9}{figure.31}\protected@file@percent }
